":" field rather than the status: this throws an ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuthError","type":"reference"},{"text":" whose","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuthError\/oauthError","type":"reference"},{"text":" carries that field, so a caller driving its own loop can tell","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"authorization_pending"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"slow_down"},{"text":" (keep going) from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"access_denied"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"expired_token"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"invalid_grant"},{"text":" (stop). The sixth, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"401"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"invalid_client"},{"text":" (contract","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"1.62), is dispatched the same way and is terminal: a failed client authentication is not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an expired session, so it is not retried and does not enter the §9 refresh guard.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"5xx"},{"text":" is a transport failure whatever its body (§14.2 rule 6, contract 1.64 amended): it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is first retried under §16 inside this call (a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"429"},{"text":" never is), then throws the §2","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/NetworkError","type":"reference"},{"text":", and the loop keeps polling. A ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"429"},{"text":" is rule 9’s wait","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whatever its body names; this call throws it as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rate_limit_exceeded"},{"text":" when the body is an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"OAuth error, and as the §2 ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/NetworkError","type":"reference"},{"text":" when it is not.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Client authentication (§14.1 rules 2 and 3)."}]},{"type":"text","text":" Every poll sends "},{"code":"client_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A client"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"configured with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamConfig\/oidcClientSecret","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" also sends it as "},{"code":"client_secret","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"form body — never as "},{"code":"Authorization: Basic","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", whatever the client is registered for — and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"client with a §6.1 certificate presents it on the connection; a public client sends"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"neither. This SDK verifies DPoP proofs but does not generate them (§21.9), so a client"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"registered for DPoP cannot be driven from here: its poll is refused "},{"code":"401 invalid_client","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and surfaces as above. A response whose "},{"code":"token_type","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"DPoP","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is surfaced as the server"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"said it ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcTokenSet\/tokenType","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), never assumed to be "},{"code":"Bearer","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient\/deviceLogin(scope:tenantID:configuration:onAuthorization:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" is the loop most callers","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"want; this exists for one that needs its own.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/AuthError":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuthError","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/autherror","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AuthError","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AuthError","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Authentication failure (§2). Carries a human-readable ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"message"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"AuthError"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The official Swift SDK for AXIAM (Access eXtended Identity and Authorization Management)."}],"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk","kind":"symbol","title":"AxiamSDK","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcConfiguration":{"title":"OidcConfiguration","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcConfiguration","abstract":[{"text":"The OIDC discovery document (§12.1), read from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/.well-known\/openid-configuration"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"OidcConfiguration"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcconfigura